(147573, 7519, 4817, '<td valign="top">This is a great photo. I''m still not sure exactly how you did it, but it looks like the glass at the back has some wine leaking out on the right hand side...? So I''m guessing that you''ve used some sort of clear plastic disc on top of the wine to hold it in place? Either that, or you placed the glasses at an angle in the freezer beforehand, and froze the wine that way. This would probably have produced a ''frosted'' effect, but I''m guessing you could get clear ice by boiling the wine beforehand, just like you can do with water.<br/><br/>Oh - I''ve just had another thought. It could be jelly!!!! Whichever way you''ve used, it''s a great illusion and deserves a 9.<br/></td>', 'This is a great photo. I''m still not sure exactly how you did it, but it looks like the glass at the back has some wine leaking out on the right hand side...? So I''m guessing that you''ve used some sort of clear plastic disc on top of the wine to hold it in place? Either that, or you placed the glasses at an angle in the freezer beforehand, and froze the wine that way. This would probably have produced a ''frosted'' effect, but I''m guessing you could get clear ice by boiling the wine beforehand, just like you can do with water.Oh - I''ve just had another thought. It could be jelly!!!! Whichever way you''ve used, it''s a great illusion and deserves a 9.', '2002-10-29 07:38:00.000000', NULL, 1),
