(148818, 7638, 772, '<td valign="top">Excellent :)  I have been wanting to try this one myeslf...  The only critique I have is that the ''planets'' here may be more effectively located closer to the bottom of the frame... the light is just a tad weak, but the concept is excellent... This is a perfect shot for learning how the manual settings on your camera work.  In a shot like this, set your camera on a tripod and compose your image.  Set your camera to fully manual exposure mode.  Set the aperture to a large F number (small aperture for greater depth of field).  Change the shutter speed until you find the correct exposure... The light source for this shot is particularly important also.  It needs to be bright :)  I think the example I have seen of this concept in the past was done with the light from a slide projector.  Great shot :) = 9 - setzler</td>', 'Excellent :)  I have been wanting to try this one myeslf...  The only critique I have is that the ''planets'' here may be more effectively located closer to the bottom of the frame... the light is just a tad weak, but the concept is excellent... This is a perfect shot for learning how the manual settings on your camera work.  In a shot like this, set your camera on a tripod and compose your image.  Set your camera to fully manual exposure mode.  Set the aperture to a large F number (small aperture for greater depth of field).  Change the shutter speed until you find the correct exposure... The light source for this shot is particularly important also.  It needs to be bright :)  I think the example I have seen of this concept in the past was done with the light from a slide projector.  Great shot :) = 9 - setzler', '2002-10-28 11:06:00.000000', NULL, 1),
